Chapter: DisplayOpsTest
  cites Kernel chapter DisplayOps
  cites Kernel chapter BitmapFont

 The Display effect operations are performable now, not unhandled effect
 operations. This program drives the four effect ops -- clear, set-pixel,
 draw-rect, draw-text -- and the full-colour palette beside them --
 fill-rect, write-text and write-text-font over a hoisted display-font --
 against the GOP framebuffer at 0xBF000000, then reads the pixels back to
 prove each one painted what it claimed and in the colour it was given.
 clear establishes a known black field, so an unpainted pixel reads 0.
 Each effectful draw is threaded through a step helper in argument
 position, the sanctioned position for an effectful call outside an
 act-bind; the boot grant from opening's own manifest supplies the
 Display capability bit. The glyph rows: 'A' (CCE 41) has row-2 byte 24 =
 0b00011000 so column 3 is lit; 'B' (CCE 58) row-2 byte 124 lights
 column 1; 'C' (CCE 50) row-2 byte 60 lights column 2.

Section: Body

  check-all : Integer -> [Display] Text
  check-all (z) =
    if peek-32 #BF000000 ((20 * 640 + 10) * 4) /= #123456 then "FAIL: set-pixel"
    else if peek-32 #BF000000 ((102 * 640 + 102) * 4) /= #FFFFFF then "FAIL: rect interior not painted"
    else if peek-32 #BF000000 ((106 * 640 + 106) * 4) /= 0 then "FAIL: rect leaked outside its bounds"
    else if peek-32 #BF000000 ((202 * 640 + 203) * 4) /= #FFFFFF then "FAIL: glyph pixel not lit"
    else if peek-32 #BF000000 ((200 * 640 + 200) * 4) /= 0 then "FAIL: glyph blank row painted"
    else if peek-32 #BF000000 ((102 * 640 + 302) * 4) /= #123456 then "FAIL: fill-rect colour wrong"
    else if peek-32 #BF000000 ((302 * 640 + 301) * 4) /= #00FF00 then "FAIL: write-text colour wrong"
    else if peek-32 #BF000000 ((302 * 640 + 322) * 4) /= #FF0000 then "FAIL: write-text-font colour wrong"
    else "PASS"

  after-wtext : Integer -> [Display] Text
  after-wtext (z) = check-all (write-text-font display-font "C" 320 300 #FF0000)

  after-fillrect : Integer -> [Display] Text
  after-fillrect (z) = after-wtext (write-text "B" 300 300 #00FF00)

  after-text : Integer -> [Display] Text
  after-text (e) = after-fillrect (fill-rect 300 100 8 8 #123456)

  after-rect : Integer -> [Display] Text
  after-rect (d) = after-text (draw-text "A" 200 200)

  after-pixel : Integer -> [Display] Text
  after-pixel (b) = after-rect (draw-rect 100 100 5 5)

  after-clear : Integer -> [Display] Text
  after-clear (a) = after-pixel (set-pixel 10 20 #123456)

  run-display : Integer -> [Display] Text
  run-display (x) = after-clear clear

  opening : [Console, Display] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (run-display 0)
  end
